Q1. When to use git reset
Use git reset when you need to undo commits by moving the branch pointer backward in commit history, whereas git restore is used to discard uncommitted file changes in your working directory or unstage files.

Q2. The three modes
The three modes of git reset are --soft, --mixed (the default), and --hard. --soft is the safest mode for preserving your changes because it moves the HEAD pointer back while keeping all your changes safely staged in the staging area.

